            {
                "entry_id": "3f65a014-a4ed-3198-9eb5-5896a4afdc73",
                "word": "daw",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6b1a1ada-90d1-4016-bcc2-687bfc0994b8",
                        "entry_id": "3f65a014-a4ed-3198-9eb5-5896a4afdc73",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "daws"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f015f304-e1c3-3d87-9417-c42bb2ad636c",
                        "entry_id": "3f65a014-a4ed-3198-9eb5-5896a4afdc73",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A western jackdaw, Coloeus monedula, a passerine bird in the crow family (Corvidae), more commonly called jackdaw."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "788568e3-b3bd-43c7-ab10-e2f5cf38ffc5",
                                "sense_id": "f015f304-e1c3-3d87-9417-c42bb2ad636c",
                                "text": "The loud daw, his throat displaying, draws\n The whole assembly of his fellow daws."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8d203881-1e01-4710-ae9a-34503f4f158f",
                                "sense_id": "f015f304-e1c3-3d87-9417-c42bb2ad636c",
                                "text": "[…] But I will wear my heart upon my sleeve\nFor daws to peck at: I am not what I am."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "208333fa-7727-34e2-ab0b-23433db1a376",
                        "entry_id": "3f65a014-a4ed-3198-9eb5-5896a4afdc73",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An idiot, a simpleton; fool."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e1077b51-3dbd-4edc-b608-fdc32a9edef9",
                                "sense_id": "208333fa-7727-34e2-ab0b-23433db1a376",
                                "text": "Therefore to make complaynt\nOf such mysadvysed\nParsons and dysgysed,\nThys boke we have devysed, […]\nNo good preest to offend,\nBut suche dawes to amend, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4f9a4c60-fe40-4e59-8593-2787a09044e2",
                                "sense_id": "208333fa-7727-34e2-ab0b-23433db1a376",
                                "text": "A kind of choughs, Or thievish daws, sir, that have pick'd my purse Of eight score and ten pounds within these five weeks"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c1b26c81-2f5b-4547-844c-5eff94330640",
                                "sense_id": "208333fa-7727-34e2-ab0b-23433db1a376",
                                "text": "‘Of course I do, you great daw.’ She kissed his beautiful mouth and moved his fringe out of his eyes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": [
                    {
